ccepts `fix` followed by whitespace and `owner/repo#N`.\n- Required-issue lookup: `src/issue-link-verification.lib.mjs` (`PARENT_FIELDS`) sends `issue(number:3929)`, which produces the GraphQL error.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\n- A reference to a pull request must never become a required issue-closing reference.\n- A PR target should be ignored for issue-link verification, or resolved as a PR and treated as non-closing.\n- Auto-merge must not be blocked with `issue_link_verification_failed` because a parsed reference is a PR.\n- The blocker text should not tell the author to add `Fixes #3929` for a PR.\n- Add a regression test for `The upstream process fix owner/repo#123 is still open.` where `#123` is a PR, and for a PR that genuinely closes an issue in another repository.\n\n## Workaround\n\n- Reword the sentence so a closing keyword does not sit immediately before the PR reference, for example: `The upstream process fix is tracked in link-assistant/hive-mind#3929.`\n- Or merge the PR manually.\n- Or avoid cross-repository PR references in PR descriptions.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\n- In `extractClosingIssueReferences`, skip references that resolve to PRs.\n- In `fetchPullRequestIssueScope` / `fetchRequiredIssueScope`, probe the target type and ignore PRs instead of calling `issue(number:)` blindly.\n- Do not fail the whole verification when one parsed reference is a PR; log it and continue.\n- Prefer GitHub's `closingIssuesReferences` as the source of truth for the final required set.\n\n\n__formal_ai_exit=0\n",
